  "id": "TR-MCP-USECASE-019",
  "description": "Resolve and validate physical filesystem identity through interruptible native handles or isolated workers whose public deadlines and accounting remain truthful; bind SQLite opening to the validated object without lexical races; attribute PostgreSQL cancellation to the actual caller cancel request; compose platform-native tests and process containment without pass-through fallbacks; and generate exact-final-HEAD evidence through a mechanically verified immutable workflow.\nConverted from FR-MCP-USECASE-017 on 2026-10-19 (operator: \"If it is in a FR, then that FR needs to be converted to a TR\"; answers \"Merge into its TR (Recommended)\" and \"FR-001, delete FRs (Recommended)\"). FR-MCP-USECASE-017 stated: Use-case persistence and its filesystem, provider, process, platform-test, and evidence boundaries shall close physical alias and replacement races, complete publicly within finite contracts, preserve truthful worker and provider causality, execute applicable native contracts, and report only exact immutable evidence while retaining every previously approved control.\n**Covered by:** FR: FR-MCP-USECASE-001; TEST: TEST-MCP-USECASE-020"
