**23 PASS, 12 FAIL, 0 UNKNOWN.** UG18 is OVERRIDDEN; UG20 is OUT OF SCOPE. The supplied gates and hashes reconcile, but three material implementation and coverage gaps remain:

- **R10-F1:** [RequirementStoredTimestamp.cs:27](/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.worktrees/unit-suite-green-20261019/src/QBrainAi.Services/Requirements/RequirementStoredTimestamp.cs:27) accepts incomplete dates because finding the parsed year in the input does not establish a complete date. For example, `October 2026` acquires day 1. Strengthen FR-MCP-040 ac-1 coverage for incomplete date components and mapping selection. This is source-derived, supported by [.NET’s parser](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dotnet/runtime/v10.0.0/src/libraries/System.Private.CoreLib/src/System/Globalization/DateTimeParse.cs).
- **R10-F2:** [TemporaryInstanceChecks.cs:380](/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.worktrees/unit-suite-green-20261019/tests/TestSupport.Shared/TemporaryInstanceChecks.cs:380) discards root identity, allowing a single-rooted path to pass containment under a UNC root. Its syntax classifier also misses forward-slash UNC case aliases. Preserve root identity and add UNC, separator and case-alias contracts.
- **R10-F3:** Six unit cases retain live-clock bounds or timestamp-order assertions after sleeps, contrary to AC-006/AC-008. One example is [StubAuthRotationHandlerTests.cs:22](/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.worktrees/unit-suite-green-20261019/tests/QBrainAi.Repl.Core.Tests/StubAuthRotationHandlerTests.cs:22). Replace their clock dependencies with fixed or scripted timestamps while preserving their state assertions.

All three are **implementer edits**. R9-F3 and R9-F4 remain incomplete; the other six round 9 findings close.

The [complete verdict](/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.worktrees/unit-suite-green-20261019/docs/receipts/hv/hostile-validator-unitgreen-r10-20261103T062131.md) and [structured receipt](/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.worktrees/unit-suite-green-20261019/docs/receipts/hv/hostile-validator-unitgreen-r10-20261103T062131.json) contain every claim, closure, exact location, proposed criterion and named test. Both were persisted completely and [verified byte for byte](/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.worktrees/unit-suite-green-20261019/docs/receipts/hv/hv-ug-r10-persistence-proof.json). No builds or tests were run; tracked files remain unchanged.

Live rollout metadata proves `gpt-6-astra`, effort `max`. The plugin reset its stored model label to `codex` during turn completion; that operational issue is recorded separately and does not affect scores.

